OpenAI chat completion  `finish_reason` does not return `function_call` but instead returns `stop` when defining the `function_call` parameter to force it to call a particular function (see repro steps below). 

Because of `finish_reason` in the last chunk being `stop` we don't run [this ](https://github.com/vercel-labs/ai/blob/main/packages/core/streams/openai-stream.ts#L157-L158) hence, the resulting string right after transform flush looks like so: 

`"{\"function_call\": {\"name\": \"log_age\", \"arguments\": \"{}"`

![image](https://github.com/vercel-labs/ai/assets/9932250/c681c7a4-a286-40ac-9d72-6fbbba756396)

[This line throws](https://github.com/vercel-labs/ai/blob/main/packages/core/streams/openai-stream.ts#L235) because the JSON is incomplete (from not adding those last two closing curly braces) and that's what this issue is all about.

Now I would argue this is more on OpenAI not fully adhering to one contract of always marking `finish_reason: function_call` when provided functions with a function_call. 

However I have lower expectations on OpenAI getting this resolved faster than we can patch it here in the meantime.  I will try my best to make another issue on one of the OpenAI repos about it.

