### Feature Description

I would like to propose a feature that allows users to obtain the total token usage directly from the client when using the useCompletion hook. Currently, it is possible to send token usage from the server to the client, but not in the same request made with useCompletion. It would be useful for usage to be a promise that resolves when the completion streaming ends, providing the usage data. This feature would improve the SDK by allowing direct access to token usage information in the client response, simplifying data management processes and enhancing efficiency.

### Use Case

In applications where tracking token usage is crucial, such as those with limited resources or cost-sensitive operations, being able to directly access token usage from the client in the same request would streamline workflows. For example, developers could monitor and display token usage in real-time without additional backend calls, providing a better user experience and more immediate feedback.


