### Feature Description

It would be very helpful if the Vercel AI SDK supported specifying [Application Inference Profiles (AIP)](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/bedrock/latest/userguide/model-customization-inference-profiles.html) when using AWS Bedrock models (such as Titan or Claude 3).

AIP allows developers to control cost-performance tradeoffs such as latency, accuracy, or cost optimization. This can be critical for production use cases that need fine-tuned control over model behavior and billing tracking.

Currently, the @vercel/ai SDK does not expose a way to configure AIP options when initializing a Bedrock client. For example, in the native AWS SDK, we can do:


```
import {
  BedrockRuntimeClient,
  InvokeModelCommand
} from '@aws-sdk/client-bedrock-runtime';

const client = new BedrockRuntimeClient({ region: 'us-east-1' });

const command = new InvokeModelCommand({
  modelId: 'amazon.titan-text-lite-v1',
  contentType: 'application/json',
  accept: 'application/json',
  body: JSON.stringify({
    inputText: "Hello!",
  }),
  // AIP Setting Like this
  inferenceConfiguration: {
    inferenceParameterOverrides: {
      profile: 'cost-optimized',
    },
  }
});

const response = await client.send(command);
```

However, in the current @vercel/ai implementation, there’s no way to specify inferenceConfiguration.

Proposed Solution:
Extend the Bedrock providers in @vercel/ai (e.g., BedrockAnthropic, BedrockTitan, etc.) to accept an optional inferenceConfiguration or profile parameter so that developers can use different AIP options.

### Use Cases

	•	Reduce latency for real-time user-facing applications
	•	Optimize cost in batch-processing jobs
	•	Tune accuracy vs speed for different product modes
	•	Company policy requires using specific AIP profiles with billing tags to enable cost attribution and usage tracking per team or project. This is critical for monitoring and auditing Bedrock usage internally.


