## Description
We rely on tool invocation states in our chatbot to render loading indicators while a tool call is executing.

This works as expected when the model outputs any text in a message before calling the tool in a subsequent step. In this case, the first tool invocation we receive is a `partial-call`:

```
{
    "part": {
        "type": "tool-invocation",
        "toolInvocation": {
            "state": "partial-call",
            "step": 0,
            "toolCallId": "call_REmGVGoRRU8QdTQwDi0aEiov",
            "toolName": "countdown"
        }
    }
}
```

But when the tool is called first – before any text is streamed – the tool invocation never enters a `call` or `partial-call` state. The first tool invocation we receive is the `result` step:

```
