### Description

🐛 Bug Report
When using @ai-sdk's streamText() with OpenAI-compatible providers like [Langdock](https://langdock.com/), the usage object in the onFinish callback contains null or undefined values for promptTokens, completionTokens, and totalTokens.

This is because Langdock returns the fields in snake_case (prompt_tokens, completion_tokens, total_tokens), while the SDK expects camelCase as per its own TokenUsage type definition.

✅ Expected Behavior
The usage object passed to onFinish should include:

`{
  promptTokens: number;
  completionTokens: number;
  totalTokens: number;
}`
even if the provider returns snake_case keys.

❌ Actual Behavior
The values in usage are null:


`onFinish: ({ usage }) => {
  console.log(usage); 
  // => { promptTokens: null, completionTokens: null, totalTokens: null }
}`

Meanwhile, inspecting the actual API response from Langdock shows:

`"usage": {
  "prompt_tokens": 14,
  "completion_tokens": 18,
  "total_tokens": 32
}`
💡 Suggested Fix
Internally normalize usage fields from snake_case to camelCase:

`usage.promptTokens = usage.promptTokens ?? usage.prompt_tokens;`

Or provide an official normalizeUsage() helper for OpenAI-compatible backends.

🛠 Temporary Workaround
We’re currently wrapping streamText() like this:

`function normalizeUsage(usage: any) {
  return {
    promptTokens: usage?.promptTokens ?? usage?.prompt_tokens ?? 0,
    completionTokens: usage?.completionTokens ?? usage?.completion_tokens ?? 0,
    totalTokens: usage?.totalTokens ?? usage?.total_tokens ?? 0,
  };
}`
🧪 Environment
@ai-sdk/core

@ai-sdk/openai

Provider: Langdock (OpenAI-compatible)

Model: gpt-4.1 / gpt-4o-mini

Node.js

TypeScript

