### Description

Thanks to @lgrammel for adding Agent swarm support in v5 as posted in https://github.com/vercel/ai/issues/3233.

We are working on implementing this in our system. However, there is one key challenge remaining which is to dynamically switch tools based on agent.

We have a multi-agent system with each agent having their own tools.

```
export const agents = [
  {
    description: 'This is the primary orchestration agent that will be used to orchestrate the other agents.',
    transfer: ['support', 'small_talk'],
    instructions: 'You are a helpful assistant that can help with a wide range of tasks.',
    name: 'orchestrator',
    tools: [],
  },
  {
    description: 'A support agent.',
    transfer: ['orchestrator'],
    instructions: 'You are an agent that specializes in providing support to users including looking up inventory.',
    name: 'support',
    tools: ['inventory_search'],
  },
  {
    description: 'A small-talk agent that is able to answer about news, weather or jokes.',
    transfer: ['orchestrator'],
    instructions: 'You are an agent that specializes in small-talk such as jokes, riddles, general knowledge, weather, etc.',
    name: 'small_talk',
    tools: ['web_search', 'display_weather'],
  },
]
```

Note, each agent has their own unique set of tools. In a large system, we can not load/know all tools to be used upfront. Therefore, we are requesting `tool` support on prepareStep. This is how I imagine it would work.

```
export async function POST(req: Request) {
  const { messages }: { messages: UIMessage[] } = await req.json()

  // Start with orchestrator as the active agent
  let activeAgent = getAgent('orchestrator')

  const result = streamText({
    messages: convertToModelMessages(messages),
    prepareStep: () => (
      {
        tools: activeAgent.tools,
        system: activeAgent.system,
      }
    ),
  })

  return result.toUIMessageStreamResponse()
}
```

This small support would help get unblocked with our swarm based agent architecture. Thank you!

