### Description

In AI SDK v4 you could use `mode: "tool"` to use a tool call instead of structured output for `generateObject`. Since the update to v5 this seems to no longer be respected and `mode: "tool" | "auto" | "json"` seems ignored, unless I'm missing something.

Reproduction:

```
streamObject({
  model: openAI('gpt-4.1-2025-04-14'),
  prompt: "Create an example list of random todo items",
  mode: "tool", // <- Important
  schema: z.object({
    list: z.array(z.string()),
  }),
})
```

With AI SDK v4 and `@ai-sdk/openai@^1` this results in the following requests:

```
{
    "model": "gpt-4.1-2025-04-14",
    "temperature": 0,
    "messages": [
        {
            "role": "user",
            "content": "Create an example list of random todo items"
        }
    ],
    "tool_choice": {
        "type": "function",
        "function": {
            "name": "json"
        }
    },
    "tools": [
        {
            "type": "function",
            "function": {
                "name": "json",
                "description": "Respond with a JSON object.",
                "parameters": {
                    "type": "object",
                    "properties": {
                        "list": {
                            "type": "array",
                            "items": {
                                "type": "string"
                            }
                        }
                    },
                    "required": [
                        "list"
                    ],
                    "additionalProperties": false,
                    "$schema": "http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#"
                }
            }
        }
    ],
    "stream": true
}
```


With `ai@5.0.2` and `@ai-sdk/openai@2.0.2` this results in a request with structured output instead regardless of the `tool` mode:

```
{
  "model": "gpt-4.1-2025-04-14",
  "input": [
    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "input_text",
          "text": "Create an example list of random todo items"
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "text": {
    "format": {
      "type": "json_schema",
      "strict": false,
      "name": "response",
      "schema": {
        "type": "object",
        "properties": {
          "list": {
            "type": "array",
            "items": {
              "type": "string"
            }
          }
        },
        "required": [
          "list"
        ],
        "additionalProperties": false,
        "$schema": "http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#"
      }
    }
  },
  "stream": true
}
```


Perhaps for the openAI provider it is recommended to always use structured output and not tool calls. 

But in `LanguageModelV2CallOptions` it seems like it is no longer possible to make the distinction between `tool` mode and `json` mode, and I noticed this regression in our project using `@openrouter/ai-sdk-provider` package (see issue https://github.com/OpenRouterTeam/ai-sdk-provider/issues/120). Where using `mode: "tool"` worked as a workaround for models that don't support the openAI standard for structured output.

So how could a provider account for this? Or is `mode: "tool"` on track to be deprecated? 

Thank you

