### Description

After our AI SDK 5 upgrade, we noticed a bug in production where the `onFinish` callback from `streamText` was returning a `responseMessage` object with all the parts properly filled in, but it had an ID with an empty string.

The reason this is problematic is because it broke all of our checks to make sure that the ID was populated. Whereas previously we would assign a UUID in the event that the response message ID wasn't present, now that check was passing, so we were trying to save messages with an empty ID.

I think if you're going to return a `responseMessage` with ID value, it should either be `null`, `undefined`, or it should be a defaulted UUID. I'll leave it on you guys to figure out, but an empty string `""` is just really bad form.

Example:

