### Description

**Background:**
We are trying to migrate our Nextjs application from AI SDK V4 to V5. In V4 we used processDataStream, mainly as a workaround because useCompletion has lacked certain callbacks that we needed to return additional metadata to the UI that we send from the route using custom data.  Our application doesn't function in the context of a "chat" interface so we have tried to avoid using useChat.  In V4 we created our own hook that does the fetch and then would provide the response.body to processDataStream/processTextStream and this worked for us.

Based on the migration guide to V5 it outlines that we need to use readUIMessageStream instead of processDataStream but the examples do not show how this can be used to handle a response object.

I was able to get it working in basic scenarios with the following:
```
const response = await fetch(stuff)

//uiMessageChunkSchema is not exposed from ai
const chunkStream = parseJsonEventStream<UIMessageChunk>({
  stream: response.body
}).pipeThrough(
  new TransformStream<ParseResult<UIMessageChunk>, UIMessageChunk>({
    transform(part, controller) {
      if (!part.success) throw part.error;
      controller.enqueue(part.value);
    },
  }),
);

for await (const message of readUIMessageStream({
  stream: chunkStream as unknown as ReadableStream<any>, 
})) {
  for (const part of message.parts) {
    if (part.type === 'text') {
      console.log('text', part.text);
    } else if (part.type === 'data-content') {
      console.log('data-content', part.data);
    }
  }
}
```
But this does not seem correct because parseJsonEventStream isn't really documented anywhere (I just looked at call-completion-api.ts) to get an idea of what it was doing.  Even if it is the correct approach, I can't get access to the uiMessageChunkSchema for the schema in parseJsonEventStream so it feels incomplete.

**What I am looking with support on:**
Either:
1. Examples of how to correctly use readUIMessageStream on the client to manually parse the stream parts.  Maybe these could be added to the V4 to V5 migration guide to assist anyone else who has similar update needs.  Which I'd be happy to contribute to.
2. Any alternative recommendations to be able to handle custom data, tool calls, etc. on the client side.  useChat works for this but adds a lot of overhead when we are not sending messages and just need to stream one-off request/responses.

