### Description

# Bug: Multiple non-transient data-* parts create separate assistant message objects in stream

## Description
When using multiple `data-*` custom data parts with `transient: false`, the backend creates separate assistant message objects in the stream instead of grouping them under the same message.

This behavior occurs even when following the example from the documentation.  
The expectation is that multiple non-transient `data-progress` parts should append under the same assistant message, but currently, each part results in a separate assistant message object.

I am intentionally not using `id` in custom streams because I want to display status messages one after another in the order they are emitted.

---

## Example

### Frontend
```tsx
'use client';

import { useChat } from '@ai-sdk/react';
import { useState } from 'react';
import type { MyUIMessage } from '@/ai/types';

export default function Chat() {
