### Description

I couldn't find anything in the docs for cross-provider model fallback control. I do see the [Custom Provider's Fallback Provider](https://ai-sdk.dev/docs/reference/ai-sdk-core/custom-provider#fallback-provider) which I don't think is relevant for what I'm trying to do.

Specifically, I would like the capabilities offered by [ai-fallback](https://github.com/remorses/ai-fallback) to be a part of ai-sdk. Something like this should be possible in ai-sdk: 

```ts
const modelWithFallbacks = createFallback({
    models: [
        gateway('broken-model'), // this will fail
        openai('gpt-4o-mini'), // this will succeed
    ],
    onError: (error, modelId) => {
        console.error(`Error with model ${modelId}:`, error)
    },
    modelResetInterval: 60000, // Reset to first model after 1 minute of the first error
})

const { text, providerMetadata } = await generateText({
      model: modelWithFallbacks,
      prompt: "Say hello in one sentence",
    });
```

---

The motivation for this is sometimes my preferred provider-model fails consistently even on retries w/ backoff. Sometimes it's a temporary provider error, other times it's the model failing to perform a task (such as producing a structured output). In these cases, I may want to try a different model or provider of the same model! And even more, I want to log which model(s) failed and why in addition to which model was the successful one.

What's more complex is that you have to make wrapped language models to use `ai-fallback`with different provider settings. I got this behavior working with the help of `ai-fallback` by using the `wrapLanguageModel` and `defaultSettingsMiddleware`:

```ts
const model1 = wrapLanguageModel({
  model: gateway("not-real-model"), // This will fail and trigger fallback
  middleware: defaultSettingsMiddleware({
    settings: {
      providerOptions: {
        gateway: {
          only: ["fireworks"], // Will be used if this model succeeds
        },
      },
    },
  }),
});

const model2 = wrapLanguageModel({
  model: gateway("gpt-oss-20b"), // Using a model that exists
  middleware: defaultSettingsMiddleware({
    settings: {
      providerOptions: {
        gateway: {
          only: ["groq"], // This will be used when fallback switches
        },
      },
    },
  }),
});

const fallbackModel = createFallback({
  models: [model1, model2],
  shouldRetryThisError: (error: Error) => {
    const statusCode = (error as any)?.statusCode;
    if (statusCode === 404 || statusCode === 400) {
      return true;
    }
    return defaultShouldRetryThisError(error);
  },
  onError: (error, modelId) => {
    console.log(`❌ Model failed: ${modelId}`);
    console.log(`   Error: ${error.message}\n`);
  },
});

const { text } = await generateText({
      model: fallbackModel,
      prompt: "Say hello in one sentence",
    });
```

