### Description

Hey, we're currently adding 'stop streaming' support to our product. The [docs](https://ai-sdk.dev/docs/advanced/stopping-streams) were helpful for this. We're using `result.toUIMessageStream` and can therefore rely on the `onFinish` callback to gives us the generated messages and the `isAborted` flag. Regardless of whether it was aborted, we just save the provided messages to the DB. In the docs, it suggests having a separate function called `savePartialResults`. We just save everything, with the assumption that the SDK can handle follow-up messages from a user where the previous messages were partial. This assumption is where we're going wrong. For Gemini and Claude, it seems to work, but only if the previous messages were text outputs. For OpenAI, it just generates an assistant message with an empty parts array, so we get a frontend error. If the interrupted message was a tool call (so the state remains as `input-available` or something), then all the providers seem to panic.

My question is how are we supposed to persist partial messages without it breaking follow-up messages? We'd rather not have to modify/fake the output. Stripping partial outputs before saving would desynchronize the client's visual conversation with the DB. I'm not sure why the models can't seem to handle a partial tool call followed by a user message, considering this is a flow I frequently perform on their own first-party chat platforms.

