### Description

## Description

AI Gateway fails with "Unsupported file uri" for Supabase signed URLs when using Gemini 3 models. This persists after upgrading to `ai@5.0.104`, despite #10349 being marked as fixed.

The same URLs work perfectly with the direct `@ai-sdk/google` provider.

## Reproduction

```typescript
import { generateText } from "ai";

// ❌ Fails with AI Gateway
const result = await generateText({
  model: "google/gemini-3-pro-image-preview",
  messages: [{
    role: "user",
    content: [
      { type: "text", text: "Describe this image" },
      { type: "image", image: "https://xxx.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/sign/..." },
    ],
  }],
  providerOptions: {
    gateway: { only: ["google"] },
  },
});
```

```typescript
import { google } from "@ai-sdk/google";

// ✅ Works with direct provider
const result = await generateText({
  model: google("gemini-3-pro-image-preview"),
  messages: [{
    role: "user", 
    content: [
      { type: "text", text: "Describe this image" },
      { type: "image", image: "https://xxx.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/sign/..." },
    ],
  }],
});
```

## Error

```
GatewayInternalServerError: Unsupported file uri: https://xxx.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/sign/...
```

## Root Cause

AI Gateway sets `supportedUrls = { "*/*": [/.*/] }`, telling the SDK all URLs are natively supported. The SDK therefore never downloads images—it passes URLs through as-is.

The direct provider only claims support for Google Files API and YouTube URLs, so the SDK downloads everything else automatically.


## Related

- #10349 - Same issue, closed as fixed, but only tested with `pexels.com` URLs

### AI SDK Version

ai: 5.0.104
@ai-sdk/google: 2.0.44
@ai-sdk/gateway: 2.0.17
@ai-sdk/react: 2.0.104

