Overview of the issue

  Issue: reasoning-end event is emitted at the wrong time

  In streaming output, when both reasoning and text content are present, the reasoning-end event is emitted at the wrong time:
```

  Actual order (incorrect):
[reasoning-start]
...reasoning content...
[text-start]
...text content...
[tool-input-start]
  ...
  [tool-call]
  [tool-result]
[reasoning-end]  ← Only issued after tool-call
  [text-end]
  [finish-step]

  Expected order:
[reasoning-start]
...reasoning content...
[reasoning-end]  ← should be before text-start
[text-start]
...text content...
[tool-input-start]
...
[tool-call]
[tool-result]
  [text-end]
  [finish-step]

```
  Reason for the problem:

In the doStream method of openai-compatible-chat-language-model.ts, the reasoning-end and text-end events are emitted uniformly during the flush() stage (lines 619-626), rather than immediately after the reasoning content ends:

```
flush(controller) {
  if (isActiveReasoning) {
    controller.enqueue({ type: 'reasoning-end', id: 'reasoning-0' });
}
    if (isActiveText) {
      controller.enqueue({ type: 'text-end', id: 'txt-0' });
    }
// ...
  }
```

  This causes the reasoning-end to be delayed until the end of the stream when reasoning ends, text begins, and then there is a tool call.

  Impact:

- The event listener cannot correctly determine when reasoning ends
- It is not possible to process subsequent logic immediately after reasoning ends
- UI rendering that needs to distinguish between reasoning and text content will have issues


