## Description

When using `@ai-sdk/google-vertex` with `generateObject`, PDF file processing fails with the error "The document has no pages" when a system message containing dynamic file-specific information (e.g., filename) is provided alongside the PDF file.

The same PDF files are processed successfully when the system message contains only generic instructions without file-specific metadata.

## Reproduction Steps

### Failing Case

```typescript
import { generateObject } from 'ai';
import { vertex } from '@ai-sdk/google-vertex';
import { z } from 'zod';

const pdfBuffer = fs.readFileSync('document.pdf');

const result = await generateObject({
  model: vertex('gemini-2.5-flash', 'us-central1'),
  schema: z.object({
    documentType: z.string(),
    documentDate: z.string().nullable(),
  }),
  messages: [
    {
      role: 'system',
      content: 'You are a document analyzer. **File name**: document.pdf', // ❌ File-specific info
    },
    {
      role: 'user',
      content: [
        { type: 'text', text: 'Please analyze this document.' },
        {
          type: 'file',
          data: pdfBuffer,
          mediaType: 'application/pdf',
          filename: 'document.pdf'
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
});

// Error: AI_APICallError: The document has no pages.
```

### Working Case

```typescript
const result = await generateObject({
  model: vertex('gemini-2.5-flash', 'us-central1'),
  schema: z.object({
    documentType: z.string(),
    documentDate: z.string().nullable(),
  }),
  messages: [
    {
      role: 'system',
      content: 'You are a document analyzer.', // ✅ Generic instruction only
    },
    {
      role: 'user',
      content: [
        {
          type: 'text',
          text: 'Please analyze this document.\n\nFile name: document.pdf' // File info in user message
        },
        {
          type: 'file',
          data: pdfBuffer,
          mediaType: 'application/pdf',
          filename: 'document.pdf'
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
});

// ✅ Success
```

### Environment

- Node.js: v24.1.0
- ai: 6.0.7
- @ai-sdk/google-vertex: 4.0.1
- @ai-sdk/google (transitive dependency): 3.0.1
- Operating System: macOS 15.1
- Model Used: gemini-2.5-pro 

## Expected Behavior

PDF files should be processed successfully regardless of whether the system message contains file-specific metadata or not.

## Actual Behavior

When the system message includes dynamic file-specific information (e.g., filename, file path), the API returns:

```sh
Error executing step: AI_APICallError: The document has no pages.
    at <anonymous> (node_modules/@ai-sdk/google/node_modules/@ai-sdk/provider-utils/src/response-handler.ts:57:16)
    at process.processTicksAndRejections (node:internal/process/task_queues:105:5)
    at async postToApi (node_modules/@ai-sdk/google/node_modules/@ai-sdk/provider-utils/src/post-to-api.ts:118:28)
    at async GoogleGenerativeAILanguageModel.doGenerate (node_modules/@ai-sdk/google/src/google-generative-ai-language-model.ts:222:9)
    at async fn (node_modules/ai/src/generate-object/generate-object.ts:339:30)
    at async <anonymous> (node_modules/ai/src/telemetry/record-span.ts:21:24)
    at async _retryWithExponentialBackoff (node_modules/ai/src/util/retry-with-exponential-backoff.ts:96:12)
    at async fn (node_modules/ai/src/generate-object/generate-object.ts:310:32)
    at async <anonymous> (node_modules/ai/src/telemetry/record-span.ts:21:24)
    at async generateObject (node_modules/ai/src/generate-object/generate-object.ts:264:12)
```

The PDF file itself is valid and contains multiple pages. The error occurs consistently with the same file that works correctly when the system message structure is changed.

## Analysis

After investigating the AI SDK source code, I found that convert-to-google-generative-ai-messages.ts converts messages to Google's format with:

```typescript
{
  systemInstruction: { parts: [{ text: 'You are... **File name**: document.pdf' }] },
  contents: [
    {
      role: 'user',
      parts: [
        { text: '...' },
        { inlineData: { mimeType: 'application/pdf', data: '<base64>' }}
      ]
    }
  ]
}
```

It appears that when systemInstruction contains file-specific dynamic information combined with inlineData (PDF), the Google Vertex AI API fails to parse the PDF correctly.

The error originates from:
1. GoogleGenerativeAILanguageModel.doGenerate() (line 222)
2. postToApi() in @ai-sdk/provider-utils (line 118)
3. Response handler in @ai-sdk/provider-utils (line 57)

This suggests the issue occurs during the API request/response handling when the specific combination of systemInstruction with file metadata and PDF inlineData is sent to Google's API.

## Workaround

Move all file-specific information from the system message to the user message:

- ❌ System message: "File name: document.pdf"
- ✅ User message: "File name: document.pdf"

Additional Context

This issue was discovered while upgrading from AI SDK v5 to v6. The same codebase worked correctly with different message structures that didn't include file metadata in system messages.

