### Description

When using `streamObject` with **Claude/Anthropic models** via `@ai-sdk/gateway`, the response is **buffered and delivered in a single chunk** instead of streaming progressively. This doesn't happen with Gemini models via gateway, nor with the direct `anthropic()` provider.

### Summary of Behaviors

| Provider             | Model             | `streamObject` Streaming     |
| -------------------- | ----------------- | ---------------------------- |
| `@ai-sdk/gateway`    | Gemini 3 Pro      | ✅ Progressive (100+ chunks) |
| `@ai-sdk/gateway`    | Claude Sonnet 4.5 | ❌ **Buffered (1 chunk)**    |
| `anthropic()` direct | Claude Sonnet 4.5 | ✅ Progressive streaming     |

**The issue:** Claude models work correctly with the direct `anthropic()` provider, but when routed through `@ai-sdk/gateway`, streaming is lost.

## Related Issue

While investigating this, we also discovered a separate bug in `@posthog/ai`'s `withTracing` wrapper that breaks when used with the direct `anthropic()` provider: https://github.com/PostHog/posthog-js/issues/2848

The two issues are related because:
- We need progressive streaming for Claude models (better UX)
- Gateway doesn't stream Claude progressively (this issue)
- So we must use direct `anthropic()` provider for streaming
- But `@posthog/ai`'s `withTracing` breaks with direct `anthropic()` (PostHog issue)

## Environment

| Package             | Version |
| ------------------- | ------- |
| `ai`                | 5.0.117 |
| `@ai-sdk/gateway`   | 2.0.24  |
| `@ai-sdk/anthropic` | 2.0.57  |
| `@ai-sdk/google`    | 2.0.52  |
| `@ai-sdk/provider`  | 2.0.1   |
| Node.js             | 20.x    |

## Test Results

We systematically tested `streamObject` with image attachments across different configurations:

| Test | Model             | Provider      | Chunks | Time | Streaming      |
| ---- | ----------------- | ------------- | ------ | ---- | -------------- |
| 1    | Gemini 3 Pro      | gateway       | 152    | 98s  | ✅ Progressive |
| 2    | Claude Sonnet 4.5 | gateway       | **1**  | 33s  | ❌ Buffered    |
| 3    | Claude Sonnet 4.5 | `anthropic()` | Many   | ~30s | ✅ Progressive |

### Test Logs

**Gemini via Gateway (works correctly):**

```text
[STREAM] Starting to iterate partialObjectStream...
[STREAM] First chunk received after 66058 ms
[STREAM] Received chunk # 10
[STREAM] Received chunk # 20
...
[STREAM] Received chunk # 150
[STREAM] partialObjectStream finished. Total chunks: 152 Time: 98105 ms
```

**Claude via Gateway (buffered - NOT streaming):**

```text
[STREAM] Starting to iterate partialObjectStream...
[STREAM] First chunk received after 33494 ms
[STREAM] partialObjectStream finished. Total chunks: 1 Time: 33505 ms
```

Note: The entire response arrives in a single chunk after 33 seconds, rather than streaming progressively over those 33 seconds.

## Setup

```typescript
import { createGateway } from "@ai-sdk/gateway";
import { anthropic } from "@ai-sdk/anthropic";
import { streamObject, convertToModelMessages } from "ai";
import { z } from "zod";

const gateway = createGateway({
  headers: {
    "http-referer": "https://example.com",
    "x-title": "MyApp",
  },
});

const providerOptions = {
  gateway: {
    order: ["bedrock"], // Using AWS Bedrock as the backend
  },
};
```

## Reproduction

```typescript
import { createGateway } from "@ai-sdk/gateway";
import { anthropic } from "@ai-sdk/anthropic";
import { streamObject, convertToModelMessages } from "ai";
import { z } from "zod";

const gateway = createGateway();

const schema = z.object({
  description: z.string(),
  elements: z.array(
    z.object({
      name: z.string(),
      purpose: z.string(),
    })
  ),
});

const messagesWithImage = [
  {
    role: "user",
    parts: [
      { type: "file", mediaType: "image/png", url: imageUrl },
      { type: "text", text: "Analyze this UI and describe its components" },
    ],
  },
];

// ✅ WORKS - Gemini via Gateway streams progressively
const geminiResult = streamObject({
  model: gateway("gemini-3-pro-preview"),
  schema,
  messages: convertToModelMessages(messagesWithImage),
  providerOptions: { gateway: { order: ["bedrock"] } },
});

let geminiChunks = 0;
for await (const chunk of geminiResult.partialObjectStream) {
  geminiChunks++;
  console.log(`Gemini chunk #${geminiChunks}:`, chunk);
}
console.log(`Total Gemini chunks: ${geminiChunks}`); // ~100-150 chunks

// ❌ DOES NOT STREAM - Claude via Gateway delivers all at once
const claudeGatewayResult = streamObject({
  model: gateway("claude-sonnet-4-5"),
  schema,
  messages: convertToModelMessages(messagesWithImage),
  providerOptions: { gateway: { order: ["bedrock"] } },
});

let claudeGatewayChunks = 0;
for await (const chunk of claudeGatewayResult.partialObjectStream) {
  claudeGatewayChunks++;
  console.log(`Claude Gateway chunk #${claudeGatewayChunks}:`, chunk);
}
console.log(`Total Claude Gateway chunks: ${claudeGatewayChunks}`); // Only 1 chunk!

// ✅ WORKS - Direct Anthropic provider streams progressively
const claudeDirectResult = streamObject({
  model: anthropic("claude-sonnet-4-5"),
  schema,
  messages: convertToModelMessages(messagesWithImage),
});

let claudeDirectChunks = 0;
for await (const chunk of claudeDirectResult.partialObjectStream) {
  claudeDirectChunks++;
  console.log(`Claude Direct chunk #${claudeDirectChunks}:`, chunk);
}
console.log(`Total Claude Direct chunks: ${claudeDirectChunks}`); // Many chunks, progressive streaming
```

## Expected Behavior

`streamObject` with Claude models via `@ai-sdk/gateway` should yield partial objects progressively as they're generated, similar to:

- Gemini models via gateway (streams correctly)
- Direct `anthropic()` provider (streams correctly)

This is important for user experience - users should see the response building up incrementally rather than waiting for the entire response to complete.

## Actual Behavior

With `@ai-sdk/gateway` + Claude models + `streamObject`:

- Response is buffered somewhere in the gateway layer
- All data arrives in a **single chunk** at the end
- User sees no progressive updates during the ~30+ second generation time
- Same request with direct `anthropic()` provider streams correctly

## Analysis

The issue appears to be in how `@ai-sdk/gateway` handles streaming responses from Anthropic/Claude models specifically:

1. **Gemini via gateway**: Streaming works perfectly, chunks arrive progressively
2. **Claude via gateway**: Streaming is lost, entire response buffered
3. **Claude via direct provider**: Streaming works perfectly

This suggests the gateway layer may be:

- Not properly forwarding streaming chunks from Bedrock/Anthropic backends
- Buffering the response before forwarding
- Missing some streaming configuration specific to Anthropic models

## Impact

This forces us to use the direct `anthropic()` provider for Claude models when progressive streaming UX is required, which:

- Bypasses the gateway's routing and fallback capabilities
- Requires managing separate provider configurations
- May not be possible in all deployment scenarios

## Workaround

Use the direct `anthropic()` provider instead of routing through the gateway:

```typescript
// Instead of:
const model = gateway("claude-sonnet-4-5");

// Use:
import { anthropic } from "@ai-sdk/anthropic";
const model = anthropic("claude-sonnet-4-5");
```

This provides proper streaming but loses gateway benefits like automatic routing and fallbacks.


