### Description

When using the OpenAI provider with the newer **Responses API**, optional parameters defined in a Zod tool schema are incorrectly populated with empty strings (`""`) if the `strict` property is omitted.

While explicitly setting `strict: false` fixes this for direct OpenAI calls, the **Vercel AI Gateway** remains broken.

>By default, strict mode is disabled. 
>https://ai-sdk.dev/docs/ai-sdk-core/tools-and-tool-calling#tool-calling

This is not the case based on my testing. 

## Impact on MCP Tools

For me this was the root cause that broke MCP tools ([arqube-mcp-server](https://github.com/SonarSource/sonarqube-mcp-server)) that worked perfectly under the Chat Completion API but they are unusable with default configs, since there is a semantic difference for omitted parameters and empty string/array values.


