### Description


`ai@6` returns `undefined` for all usage token fields (`inputTokens`, `outputTokens`, `totalTokens`). Works fine with `ai@5`.

## Root Cause

It seems like the gateway backend returns usage in V2 format (flat numbers) regardless of the spec version header:

```bash
curl -s "https://ai-gateway.vercel.sh/v1/ai/language-model" \
  -H "Authorization: Bearer $AI_GATEWAY_API_KEY" \
  -H "ai-gateway-auth-method: api-key" \
  -H "ai-gateway-protocol-version: 0.0.1" \
  -H "ai-language-model-specification-version: 3" \
  -H "ai-language-model-id: openai/gpt-4o-mini" \
  -H "ai-language-model-streaming: false" \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -d '{"prompt":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Say hi"}]}]}' \
  | jq '.usage'

# Output (identical for spec version 2 and 3):
# {
#   "inputTokens": 9,
#   "outputTokens": 11,
#   "totalTokens": 20,
#   "reasoningTokens": 0,
#   "cachedInputTokens": 0
# }
```

Since `@ai-sdk/gateway` v3 declares `specificationVersion: "v3"`, `ai@6` assumes usage is already in V3 format and skips [`convertV2UsageToV3()`](https://github.com/vercel/ai/blob/32be973f7f70fea5bab1fa0cb393f95db1267503/packages/ai/src/model/as-language-model-v3.ts#L16-L18).

```typescript
// ai@6 — src/model/as-language-model-v3.ts
function asLanguageModelV3(model) {
  if (model.specificationVersion === "v3") {
    return model;  // ← skips conversion
  }
  // ... wraps with convertV2UsageToV3()
}
```

## Reproduction

```typescript
import { generateText, createGateway } from "ai";

const gateway = createGateway({
  apiKey: process.env.AI_GATEWAY_API_KEY!,
  baseURL: "https://ai-gateway.vercel.sh/v1/ai",
});

const result = await generateText({
  model: gateway("openai/gpt-4o-mini"),
  prompt: "Say hi",
});

console.log(result.usage);
// ai@5: { inputTokens: 9, outputTokens: 11, totalTokens: 20, ... }
// ai@6: { inputTokenDetails: {}, outputTokenDetails: {} }  ← all undefined
```

## Workaround

Override `specificationVersion` to `"v2"` so `ai@6` runs the V2→V3 conversion:

```typescript
const model = gateway("openai/gpt-4o-mini");
(model as any).specificationVersion = "v2";
```

