## Problem

The AI SDK's tool calling system (`tool()`, `generateText`, `streamText`) executes tools on behalf of users but doesn't produce cryptographic evidence of what was executed. As AI SDK apps move into production for enterprise and commerce use cases, verifiable action provenance becomes a requirement.

## Use case

```typescript
const result = await generateText({
  model: openai('gpt-4o'),
  tools: {
    getWeather: tool({
      execute: async ({ city }) => {
        const weather = await fetchWeather(city);
        // No proof this tool ran, what it received, or what it returned
        return weather;
      },
    }),
  },
});
```

## Proposal

Add optional receipt generation to tool execution via [Agent Action Receipts (AAR)](https://github.com/Cyberweasel777/agent-action-receipt-spec):

```typescript
import { createReceipt } from 'botindex-aar';

const result = await generateText({
  model: openai('gpt-4o'),
  tools: {
    getWeather: tool({
      execute: async ({ city }) => fetchWeather(city),
      // New: receipt generation
      receipt: {
        signingKey: process.env.RECEIPT_SIGNING_KEY,
        agentId: 'my-app/weather-agent',
      },
    }),
  },
});

// result.toolResults[0].receipt → Ed25519-signed receipt
// Verifiable by any party with the public key
```

### What AAR provides

- Ed25519 signature over canonicalized JSON per tool call
- SHA-256 input/output hashing (verifiable without exposing raw data)
- Receipt chaining across multi-step tool calls
- Compatible with Mastercard [Verifiable Intent](https://www.mastercard.com/us/en/news-and-trends/stories/2026/verifiable-intent.html) and [x402 (Coinbase)](https://github.com/coinbase/x402)

### SDK

`npm install botindex-aar` — zero-config, single dependency, MIT. Already used in production.

- Spec: https://github.com/Cyberweasel777/agent-action-receipt-spec
- Landing: https://aar.botindex.dev

