### Description

We're seeing three distinct intermittent error types from `@ai-sdk/gateway` in production, affecting all models (OpenAI, Gemini, Anthropic). These are not rate-limit or quota errors — they happen under normal production load (~50-100 concurrent AI calls) and affect both `generateText` and `ToolLoopAgent` tool-loop workflows.

### Error types observed

**1. GatewayResponseError** (related to #9579)
```
GatewayResponseError: Invalid error response format: Gateway request failed
  at Object.doGenerate (gateway-language-model.ts)
```

**2. GatewayTimeoutError / HeadersTimeoutError**
```
GatewayTimeoutError: Gateway request timed out: Cannot connect to API: Headers Timeout Error
  This is a client-side timeout. To resolve this, increase your timeout configuration.
  at Function.createTimeoutError (@ai-sdk/gateway/src/errors/gateway-timeout-error.ts:52:12)
  at asGatewayError (@ai-sdk/gateway/src/errors/as-gateway-error.ts:49:34)
  at GatewayLanguageModel.doGenerate (@ai-sdk/gateway/src/gateway-language-model.ts:91:19)
```
This happens even with `timeout: { stepMs: 90_000 }` (90s). The error fires in ~900ms suggesting the gateway itself is rejecting/dropping connections, not a real timeout.

**3. AbortError**
```
AbortError: This operation was aborted
  cause: AbortError: This operation was aborted
```

### Reproduction script

Self-contained stress test. Errors are intermittent — may need multiple runs or higher concurrency to trigger.

```bash
