### Description

In this repro our goal is to intentionally trigger Anthropic 400 validation error on **both AI SDK and AI Gateway**. This error is thrown by Anthropic when strict mode is on and tools/schema are too many or too complex. So in a way the error confirms that the strict mode is actually working.

```text
The compiled grammar is too large, which would cause performance issues. Simplify your tool schemas or reduce the number of strict tools.
```

When I run the same `streamText` call with the same `strict: true` tool definitions:
- direct Anthropic returns `400 invalid_request_error`
- the same request through Vercel AI Gateway succeeds

I built some dummy repro that setup the env and compare:

- direct Anthropic: `claude-sonnet-4-6`
- AI Gateway (limited only to anthropic): `anthropic/claude-sonnet-4.6`

The repro is intentionally small and uses dummy tool names plus plain Zod schemas. There is no specific runtime logic involved.

The prompt used is intentionally simple: `Reply with exactly "hello". Do not call any tools.` because the Anthropic error arises as soon as the tools gets loaded.

