### Description

**Background:**
When using `generateText` with the `@ai-sdk/open-responses` provider, `file` parts that are not images (e.g., `application/pdf`) are silently dropped from the request body. The SDK logs a warning (`unsupported file content type`), but the resulting API request is sent without the file data, often causing the model to respond that no document was provided.

**Reproduction Example:**

```typescript
import { createOpenResponses } from "@ai-sdk/open-responses";
import { generateText } from "ai";

const openResponses = createOpenResponses({
  name: "my-provider",
  url: "https://api.your-provider.com/v1/responses",
  apiKey: "your-api-key",
  // Log request to see the missing part
  fetch: async (url, init) => {
    console.log("Request Body:", JSON.stringify(JSON.parse(init.body as string), null, 2));
    return fetch(url, init);
  }
});

const model = openResponses("your-multimodal-model");

// Minimal PDF (Hello World)
const pdfBase64 = "";

const { text } = await generateText({
  model,
  messages: [
    {
      role: "user",
      content: [
        { type: "text", text: "What does this PDF say?" },
        { 
          type: "file", 
          data: Buffer.from(pdfBase64, "base64"), 
          mediaType: "application/pdf" 
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
});

console.log("Model response:", text);
```

**Observed Output:**
1.  **Console Warning:** `AI SDK Warning (my-provider.responses / your-multimodal-model): unsupported file content type: application/pdf`
2.  **Request Body (Logged):** The `content` array for the user message only contains the `input_text` part. The `input_file` (or `input_document`) part is missing.
3.  **Model Response:** "There is no document provided, so I have nothing to summarize."

**Technical Root Cause:**
The mapping logic in `convertToOpenResponsesInput` (found in `packages/open-responses/src/responses/convert-to-open-responses-input.ts`) has a hard-coded check:

```typescript
if (!part.mediaType.startsWith("image/")) {
  warnings.push({
    type: "other",
    message: `unsupported file content type: ${part.mediaType}`
  });
  break; 
}
```

**Suggested Fix:**
The OpenAI Responses API supports non-image files via the `input_file` part. The SDK should be updated to allow non-image media types and map them to the appropriate `input_file` structure rather than breaking out of the loop and dropping the content.


