## Summary

I'd like to propose a new example demonstrating how to build an **emotionally aware AI agent** using the AI SDK's middleware system with [`psyche-ai`](https://www.npmjs.com/package/psyche-ai) (v9, MIT, zero dependencies).

**psyche-ai** is a virtual endocrine system for AI agents — it maintains a chemical state (dopamine, serotonin, cortisol, oxytocin, norepinephrine, endorphins) that shifts in response to conversational stimuli, giving agents persistent emotional continuity across turns. It ships a first-class Vercel AI SDK adapter via `psyche-ai/vercel-ai`.

## What the example demonstrates

1. **AI SDK Middleware** — uses `wrapLanguageModel` + custom middleware (the recommended extension pattern)
2. **Emotional continuity** — the agent's internal state evolves across turns, not just per-message
3. **Observable state** — logs the chemical shifts so developers can see the system working

This is a good fit for the examples directory because it shows a real-world middleware use case beyond caching or logging — it modifies both the system prompt (injecting emotional context) and processes the output (updating internal state).

## Proposed example code

A minimal ~35-line script using `generateText` + `wrapLanguageModel`:

```typescript
// examples/ai-functions/src/generate-text/psyche-emotional-agent.ts
//
// Emotionally Aware Agent — psyche-ai + Vercel AI SDK
//
// An AI agent with a virtual endocrine system. Its internal chemistry
// (dopamine, serotonin, cortisol, oxytocin) shifts in response to
// conversational stimuli, giving it persistent emotional continuity.
//
// Run: pnpm tsx src/generate-text/psyche-emotional-agent.ts

import { generateText, wrapLanguageModel } from "ai";
import { anthropic } from "@ai-sdk/anthropic";
import { PsycheEngine, MemoryStorageAdapter } from "psyche-ai";
import { psycheMiddleware } from "psyche-ai/vercel-ai";

// 1. Create an agent with personality + in-memory state
const engine = new PsycheEngine(
  { mbti: "INFJ", name: "Echo", mode: "companion" },
  new MemoryStorageAdapter(),
);
await engine.initialize();

// 2. Wrap any AI SDK model with psyche middleware
//    This injects emotional context into the system prompt
//    and updates internal chemistry from the LLM's response.
const model = wrapLanguageModel({
  model: anthropic("claude-sonnet-4-20250514"),
  middleware: psycheMiddleware(engine),
});

// 3. Chat helper
async function chat(userMessage: string) {
  const { text } = await generateText({ model, prompt: userMessage });

  const state = engine.getState().current;
  console.log(`\nUser: ${userMessage}`);
  console.log(`Echo: ${text}`);
  console.log(
    `Chemistry: DA=${state.DA.toFixed(0)} HT=${state.HT.toFixed(0)} ` +
    `CORT=${state.CORT.toFixed(0)} OT=${state.OT.toFixed(0)}`
  );
  return text;
}

// 4. Watch the emotional arc across a conversation
await chat("You're doing amazing work!");       // praise → dopamine spike
await chat("Actually, that was terrible.");      // criticism → cortisol spike
await chat("I'm sorry, I didn't mean that.");   // repair → recovery
```

