### Description

`BedrockChatLanguageModel.doStream()` and `doGenerate()` do not return a `request` field in their return objects. This means consumers that rely on the request body (e.g., for observability, tracing, or debugging) receive `undefined`.

There is an existing `// TODO request?` comment in the source at the `doStream` return statement ([`bedrock-chat-language-model.ts` L682](https://github.com/vercel/ai/blob/main/packages/amazon-bedrock/src/bedrock-chat-language-model.ts#L682)), indicating this was a known gap.

### Impact

Observability frameworks like [Mastra](https://github.com/mastra-ai/mastra) use the `request` field from `doStream()`/`doGenerate()` to populate tracing span inputs (e.g., `model_step.input`). When using the Bedrock provider, this field is always `undefined`, which results in empty `{}` span attributes — making it impossible to see what messages/context were sent to the LLM.

The `@ai-sdk/anthropic` provider correctly returns `request: { body }` from both methods ([ref](https://github.com/vercel/ai/blob/main/packages/anthropic/src/anthropic-messages-language-model.ts)), so this only affects the Bedrock provider.

### Code example

```typescript
import { createAmazonBedrock } from '@ai-sdk/amazon-bedrock';
import { streamText } from 'ai';

const bedrock = createAmazonBedrock({ region: 'us-east-1' });

const result = streamText({
  model: bedrock('us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-6-v1'),
  messages: [{ role: 'user', content: 'Hello' }],
  onFinish: ({ request }) => {
    console.log(request.body); // undefined — should contain the Bedrock Converse API request body
  },
});
```

### Expected behavior

Both `doGenerate()` and `doStream()` should return `request: { body: args }` (where `args` is the command object passed to the Bedrock Converse API), matching the behavior of `@ai-sdk/anthropic`.

`doGenerate` currently returns:
```typescript
return {
  content,
  finishReason: { ... },
  usage: convertBedrockUsage(response.usage),
  response: { ... },
  warnings,
};
// Missing: request: { body: args }
```

`doStream` currently returns:
```typescript
return {
  stream: response.pipeThrough(...),
  // TODO request?
  response: { headers: responseHeaders },
};
// Missing: request: { body: args }
```

