### Description

Hi, I am building agents with the amazon bedrock provider, but I can't get them to work with custom application inference profile ARNs. See details below:

## Description

`@ai-sdk/amazon-bedrock` (v4.0.85) cannot be used with [AWS Bedrock application inference profiles](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/bedrock/latest/userguide/inference-profiles-create.html). Passing an inference profile ARN as the model ID results in a `400 The provided model identifier is invalid` error from the Bedrock API.

For example:

```
arn:aws:bedrock:us-east-1:123456789012:application-inference-profile/abc123xyz
```

## Potential Root Cause

The provider constructs REST API URLs by interpolating the model ID into the URL path using `encodeURIComponent`:

```typescript
// bedrock-chat-language-model.ts:963-966
private getUrl(modelId: string) {
  const encodedModelId = encodeURIComponent(modelId);
  return `${this.config.baseUrl()}/model/${encodedModelId}`;
}
```

For a standard model ID like `us.amazon.nova-2-lite-v1:0`, this produces a valid URL:

```
https://bedrock-runtime.us-east-1.amazonaws.com/model/us.amazon.nova-2-lite-v1%3A0
```

For an inference profile ARN, `encodeURIComponent` encodes the slashes and colons, producing:

```
https://bedrock-runtime.us-east-1.amazonaws.com/model/arn%3Aaws%3Abedrock%3Aus-east-1%3A123456789012%3Aapplication-inference-profile%2Fabc123xyz
```

Bedrock's REST API does not accept this — the ARN must be passed **unencoded** in the URL path. The same `encodeURIComponent` pattern is also used in:

- `bedrock-image-model.ts` (line 41)
- `bedrock-embedding-model.ts` (line 42)
- `bedrock-anthropic-provider.ts` (line 259) via `buildRequestUrl`

## Reproduction

```typescript
import { createAmazonBedrock } from "@ai-sdk/amazon-bedrock";
import { generateText } from "ai";

const bedrock = createAmazonBedrock({ region: "us-east-1" });

// This works:
const result1 = await generateText({
  model: bedrock("us.amazon.nova-2-lite-v1:0"),
  prompt: "Say hello",
});

// This fails with "The provided model identifier is invalid":
const result2 = await generateText({
  model: bedrock("arn:aws:bedrock:us-east-1:123456789012:application-inference-profile/abc123xyz"),
  prompt: "Say hello",
});
```

## Workaround

I ended up building my own LanguageModelV3 implementation using the @aws-sdk/client-bedrock-runtime package, and when I provide the unencoded ARN it works just fine. 

