## Bug Report

### Description

In `runToolsTransformation`, there's a race condition between the async `transform` function processing a `tool-call` chunk and the `flush` function closing the `toolResultsStream`. The `outstandingToolResults` counter is incremented **after** an `await parseToolCall()`, but `flush` can fire during that await and see `outstandingToolResults.size === 0`, closing the stream prematurely. Tool results are then lost.

### Reproduction

This manifests when the runtime's TransformStream implementation fires `flush()` while an async `transform()` is still awaiting. We observed this consistently in Bun v1.3.11 when synchronous I/O (SQLite reads) in tool registration paths affects microtask scheduling.

### Trace Evidence

```
[transform] tool-call pending: 1      ← transform starts processing tool-call
[flush] pending: 0 outstanding: 0     ← flush fires, outstanding is still 0!
[CLOSING] toolResultsStream           ← stream closes prematurely
[tool START] bash outstanding: 1      ← tool registers AFTER stream closed
[tool RESOLVED] bash type: tool-result ← result has nowhere to go
→ "Tool execution aborted"
```

The tool executes successfully and returns a result, but the result is never delivered to the consumer because `toolResultsStream` was already closed.

### Root Cause

In `runToolsTransformation` (ai/dist/index.mjs):

```javascript
case "tool-call": {
  try {
    const toolCall = await parseToolCall(...)  // ← flush can fire during this await
    // ...
    toolInputs.set(toolCall.toolCallId, toolCall.input);
    if (tool2.execute != null && toolCall.providerExecuted !== true) {
      const toolExecutionId = generateId2();
      outstandingToolResults.add(toolExecutionId);  // ← too late, flush already closed
      executeToolCall({...}).then(result => {
        toolResultsStreamController.enqueue(result);  // ← controller already closed
      })
    }
  }
}
```

And in `flush`:
```javascript
flush() {
  canClose = true;
  attemptClose();  // closes if outstandingToolResults.size === 0
}
```

### Suggested Fix

Increment `outstandingToolResults` **before** the `await parseToolCall()`:

```javascript
case "tool-call": {
  const toolExecutionId = generateId2();
  outstandingToolResults.add(toolExecutionId);  // reserve slot BEFORE any await
  try {
    const toolCall = await parseToolCall(...)
    // ...
    if (tool2.execute != null && toolCall.providerExecuted !== true) {
      executeToolCall({...}).then(...).finally(() => {
        outstandingToolResults.delete(toolExecutionId);
        attemptClose();
      })
    } else {
      outstandingToolResults.delete(toolExecutionId);
      attemptClose();
    }
  } catch (error) {
    outstandingToolResults.delete(toolExecutionId);
    attemptClose();
    toolResultsStreamController.enqueue({ type: "error", error });
  }
}
```

This ensures `flush` → `attemptClose` always sees `outstandingToolResults.size > 0` while a tool-call chunk is being processed.

### Environment

- AI SDK version: 6.0.149
- Runtime: Bun 1.3.11 (Linux x64)
- The issue is timing-dependent and may not reproduce in Node.js if Node's TransformStream implementation strictly serializes transform/flush

