### Description

## Bug

  When a tool UI part has `state: "output-available"` but no `input` field (e.g. a tool
  that takes no parameters), `convertToModelMessages` produces a `tool-call` ModelMessage
  without `input`. The OpenAI provider then sends this to the API without `arguments`, and
  OpenAI rejects with:

  > Missing required parameter: 'input[N].arguments'

  This breaks chat history replay — once such a message is persisted and replayed, the
  conversation is permanently stuck.

  ## Reproduction

  ```ts
  import { convertToModelMessages, streamText } from 'ai'
  import { createGateway } from '@ai-sdk/gateway'
  import { z } from 'zod'

  const gateway = createGateway({ apiKey: 'YOUR_KEY' })

  const tools = {
    list_connections: {
      description: 'List connections',
      parameters: z.object({ filter: z.string().optional() }),
    },
  }

  const uiMessages = [
    {
      role: 'user' as const,
      id: '1',
      parts: [{ type: 'text' as const, text: 'list connections' }],
    },
    {
      role: 'assistant' as const,
      id: '2',
      parts: [
        {
          type: 'tool-list_connections' as const,
          toolCallId: 'call_abc',
          state: 'output-available' as const,
          // input is MISSING — tool had no parameters
          output: { connections: [{ name: 'db1' }] },
        },
        { type: 'text' as const, text: 'Here are your connections.' },
      ],
    },
    {
      role: 'user' as const,
      id: '3',
      parts: [{ type: 'text' as const, text: 'thanks' }],
    },
  ]

  const modelMessages = await convertToModelMessages(uiMessages as any, {
    tools,
    ignoreIncompleteToolCalls: true,
  })

  // This produces:
  // { type: "tool-call", toolCallId: "call_abc", toolName: "list_connections" }
  // Note: NO `input` field!

  const result = streamText({
    model: gateway('openai/gpt-4o-mini'),
    messages: modelMessages,
    tools,
  })

  // OpenAI rejects: "Missing required parameter: 'input[2].arguments'"
  ```

  ## Expected behavior

  `convertToModelMessages` should default missing `input` to `{}`:

  ```js
  // dist/index.js line ~8501, inside convertToModelMessages
  // Current:
  input: part.state === "output-error" ? ... : part.input,
  // Fixed:
  input: (part.state === "output-error" ? ... : part.input) ?? {},
  ```

  ## Why this happens

  Tools with no parameters (e.g. `list_connections`) may have their UI part persisted
  without an `input` field. When the conversation is replayed from a database, `part.input`
   is `undefined`. The `ignoreIncompleteToolCalls` flag doesn't help because the part has
  `state: "output-available"` — it looks "complete" to the SDK.

  ## Related issues

  - #5658 — `streamText` can't use tools with no arguments (streaming path)
  - #7097 — Incomplete tool input breaking chat history
  - #11406 — `safeValidateUIMessages` strips `rawInput` from `output-error` parts

  This is the same class of bug but specifically for the `output-available` state where
  `input` was never set.

