### Description

When using `streamFunctionCallArguments: true` with Vertex AI (Gemini 3 Flash), tool calls with **array-typed arguments** never produce a `tool-call` event. The `tool-input-start` and `tool-input-delta` events fire correctly, but `tool-input-end` and `tool-call` are never emitted. The tool's `execute` function is never called.

Simple tool args (e.g. `{ message: string }`) work correctly.

### Root Cause

The Vertex API's terminal streaming chunk for array args has `partialArgs` with the last value but **omits `willContinue`** (instead of setting it to `false` or sending a separate empty chunk):

```json
// Second-to-last chunk — has willContinue: true
{ "partialArgs": [{ "jsonPath": "$.operations[1].itemid", "stringValue": "" }], "willContinue": true }

// Last chunk — has partialArgs but NO willContinue field
{ "partialArgs": [{ "jsonPath": "$.operations[1].price", "numberValue": 0.5 }] }
```

The provider's `isTerminalChunk` check ([google-generative-ai-language-model.ts](https://github.com/vercel/ai/blob/main/packages/google/src/google-generative-ai-language-model.ts)) requires ALL of `name`, `args`, `partialArgs`, AND `willContinue` to be null:

```js
const isTerminalChunk = part.functionCall.name == null 
  && part.functionCall.args == null 
  && part.functionCall.partialArgs == null  // ← fails, partialArgs is present
  && part.functionCall.willContinue == null;
```

This never matches because the last chunk still has `partialArgs`. For simple args, the API sends a separate empty terminal chunk, but for array args it doesn't.

### Suggested Fix

Treat a chunk as terminal when `willContinue` is absent/undefined (not explicitly `true`) AND the chunk has `partialArgs`. Process the final `partialArgs` AND finalize the tool call in one step:

```js
const isTerminalChunk = 
  (part.functionCall.willContinue == null && part.functionCall.name == null && part.functionCall.args == null && part.functionCall.partialArgs == null) ||
  (part.functionCall.willContinue == null && part.functionCall.partialArgs != null); // last chunk with data
```

### Code example

```typescript
const result = streamText({
  model: vertex("gemini-3-flash-preview"),
  messages: [{ role: "user", content: "List 2 fruits with prices. Use write_items." }],
  tools: {
    write_items: tool({
      description: "Write items",
      inputSchema: z.object({
        operations: z.array(z.object({
          action: z.enum(["add"]),
          itemid: z.string(),
          description: z.string(),
          price: z.number(),
        })),
      }),
      execute: async ({ operations }) => {
        console.log("EXECUTE:", operations.length); // Never called
        return operations.length + " items";
      },
    }),
  },
  providerOptions: { google: { streamFunctionCallArguments: true } },
});

for await (const part of result.fullStream) {
  console.log(part.type);
  // Outputs: start, start-step, tool-input-start, tool-input-delta (x many), finish-step, finish
  // Missing: tool-input-end, tool-call, tool-result
}
```

