### Description

When using `streamText(...).toUIMessageStream({ sendReasoning: false })`, only `reasoning-delta` chunks are suppressed. The `reasoning-start` and `reasoning-end` chunks are **always enqueued** regardless of the `sendReasoning` flag.

This is a problem because providers like OpenRouter attach the full reasoning summary text inside `providerMetadata` on `reasoning-start` and `reasoning-end` events, effectively leaking the entire reasoning content to the client.

### Reproduction

```ts
const stream = streamText({
  model: openrouter("openai/o4-mini"),
  messages: [{ role: "user", content: "hello" }],
  providerOptions: {
    openai: { reasoningEffort: "medium" }
  }
});

writer.merge(
  stream.toUIMessageStream({ sendReasoning: false })
);
```

**Expected:** No reasoning-related SSE events are sent to the client.

**Actual:** Client receives:

```
data: {"type":"reasoning-start","id":"...","providerMetadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.summary","summary":"<full reasoning text>", ...}]}}}

data: {"type":"reasoning-end","id":"...","providerMetadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[...hundreds of summary chunks...]}}}
```

### Root cause

In `toUIMessageStream`, the transform only checks `sendReasoning` for `reasoning-delta`:

```js
// reasoning-start — always enqueued, no guard
case "reasoning-start": {
  controller.enqueue({
    type: "reasoning-start",
    id: part.id,
    ...part.providerMetadata != null ? { providerMetadata: part.providerMetadata } : {}
  });
  break;
}

// reasoning-delta — correctly gated
case "reasoning-delta": {
  if (sendReasoning) {  // ✅ only this one is checked
    controller.enqueue({ ... });
  }
  break;
}

// reasoning-end — always enqueued, no guard
case "reasoning-end": {
  controller.enqueue({
    type: "reasoning-end",
    id: part.id,
    ...part.providerMetadata != null ? { providerMetadata: part.providerMetadata } : {}
  });
  break;
}
```

### Suggested fix

Wrap `reasoning-start` and `reasoning-end` cases with the same `sendReasoning` guard:

```js
case "reasoning-start": {
  if (sendReasoning) {
    controller.enqueue({
      type: "reasoning-start",
      id: part.id,
      ...part.providerMetadata != null ? { providerMetadata: part.providerMetadata } : {}
    });
  }
  break;
}

case "reasoning-end": {
  if (sendReasoning) {
    controller.enqueue({
      type: "reasoning-end",
      id: part.id,
      ...part.providerMetadata != null ? { providerMetadata: part.providerMetadata } : {}
    });
  }
  break;
}
```

### Workaround

Pipe the stream through a `TransformStream` that drops all reasoning chunks manually:

```ts
const uiStream = stream.toUIMessageStream({ sendReasoning: false, ... });

const filtered = uiStream.pipeThrough(
  new TransformStream({
    transform(chunk, controller) {
      if (chunk.type === "reasoning-start" || chunk.type === "reasoning-delta" || chunk.type === "reasoning-end") return;
      controller.enqueue(chunk);
    }
  })
);

writer.merge(filtered);
```

### Environment

- `ai`: `^6.0.161`
- `@openrouter/ai-sdk-provider`: `^2.6.0`
- Model: `openai/o4-mini` via OpenRouter

