### Description

OpenAI-compatible streaming tool calls can fail when a provider/model sends the first `tool_calls` delta with an `id` and `function.arguments`, but without `function.name`, and then sends `function.name` in a later delta.

A parser that validates `function.name` on the first partial tool-call delta throws before it has a chance to accumulate the later chunk that contains the name.

This is similar to #6687 in that a provider-specific OpenAI-compatible streaming shape is valid after accumulation, but fails because the parser expects a more complete tool-call shape too early. The difference is that #6687 was about empty arguments (`""`) for parameterless tools; this issue is about `function.name` arriving after an earlier arguments-only delta.

### Expected Behavior

The streamed deltas should be accumulated by tool-call `index` / `id` until both the tool name and arguments are available.

The chunks below should become one valid tool call:

```json
{
  "id": "call_123",
  "type": "function",
  "function": {
    "name": "bash",
    "arguments": "{\"command\": \"ls -la\"}"
  }
}
```

The tool call should then be emitted/executed normally.

### Actual Behavior

The stream parser rejects the second chunk before the later `function.name` chunk is processed:

```txt
AI_InvalidResponseDataError: Expected 'function.name' to be a string.
```

### Minimal Reproduction

This mock OpenAI-compatible SSE stream reproduces the chunk ordering. The key part is the second chunk: it contains `id`, `type`, and `function.arguments`, but no `function.name`. The third chunk then provides `function.name`.

```ts
const chunks = [
  `data: {"choices":[{"finish_reason":null,"index":0,"delta":{"role":"assistant","content":null}}]}`,
  `data: {"choices":[{"finish_reason":null,"index":0,"delta":{"tool_calls":[{"index":0,"id":"call_123","type":"function","function":{"arguments":""}}]}}]}`,
  `data: {"choices":[{"finish_reason":null,"index":0,"delta":{"tool_calls":[{"index":0,"id":"call_123","type":"function","function":{"name":"bash","arguments":"{"}}]}}]}`,
  `data: {"choices":[{"finish_reason":null,"index":0,"delta":{"tool_calls":[{"index":0,"function":{"arguments":"\\u0022command\\u0022"}}]}}]}`,
  `data: {"choices":[{"finish_reason":null,"index":0,"delta":{"tool_calls":[{"index":0,"function":{"arguments":": \\u0022ls -la\\u0022}"}}]}}]}`,
  `data: {"choices":[{"finish_reason":"tool_calls","index":0,"delta":{}}]}`,
  `data: [DONE]`,
]

const response = new Response(
  new ReadableStream({
    start(controller) {
      for (const chunk of chunks) {
        controller.enqueue(new TextEncoder().encode(`${chunk}\n\n`))
      }
      controller.close()
    },
  }),
  {
    status: 200,
    headers: { "Content-Type": "text/event-stream" },
  },
)
```

A minimal provider test can mock `fetch` to return this `response` from a `/chat/completions` request and then call `streamText` with a `bash` tool. The parser should not fail on the second chunk; it should wait until the third chunk supplies `function.name` and continue accumulating arguments.

### Raw SSE Stream

```txt
data: {"choices":[{"finish_reason":null,"index":0,"delta":{"role":"assistant","content":null}}]}

data: {"choices":[{"finish_reason":null,"index":0,"delta":{"tool_calls":[{"index":0,"id":"call_123","type":"function","function":{"arguments":""}}]}}]}

data: {"choices":[{"finish_reason":null,"index":0,"delta":{"tool_calls":[{"index":0,"id":"call_123","type":"function","function":{"name":"bash","arguments":"{"}}]}}]}

data: {"choices":[{"finish_reason":null,"index":0,"delta":{"tool_calls":[{"index":0,"function":{"arguments":"\\u0022command\\u0022"}}]}}]}

data: {"choices":[{"finish_reason":null,"index":0,"delta":{"tool_calls":[{"index":0,"function":{"arguments":": \\u0022ls -la\\u0022}"}}]}}]}

data: {"choices":[{"finish_reason":"tool_calls","index":0,"delta":{}}]}

data: [DONE]
```

### Suggested Fix Direction

Accumulate partial tool-call deltas by `index` / `id` and delay validation/emission until `function.name` is available. If the stream finishes and a pending tool call still has no `function.name`, then it should remain an invalid response.

### Related

- Similar OpenAI-compatible tool-call parser issue: #6687
- Downstream report with captured local-model stream: https://github.com/anomalyco/opencode/issues/6649

### Summary

  A single `onError` callback passed to `result.toUIMessageStream({ onError })` is invoked **twice** per upstream error. The [public reference](https://ai-sdk.dev/docs/reference/ai-sdk-core/stream-text) only specifies the signature (`(error: unknown) => string`) and says it's "invoked when an error occurs during stream processing" – call frequency is not documented.

### How to reproduce

```ts
import { streamText, simulateReadableStream } from "ai";
import { MockLanguageModelV3 } from "ai/test";

const model = new MockLanguageModelV3({
  doStream: async () => ({
    stream: simulateReadableStream({
      chunks: [
        { type: "stream-start", warnings: [] },
        { type: "error", error: new Error("simulated upstream error") },
      ],
    }),
  }),
});

let calls = 0;

const result = streamText({
  model,
  prompt: "trigger error",
});

const uiStream = result.toUIMessageStream({
  onError: (err) => {
    calls += 1;
    console.log(`\n=== onError call #${calls} ===`);
    console.trace("stack");
    return (err as Error)?.message ?? String(err);
  },
  // Removing onFinish (and onStepFinish) makes handleUIMessageStreamFinish
  // early-return, which skips processUIMessageStream — onError then fires
  // only once. Keep it here to reproduce the double call.
  onFinish: () => {},
});

async function main() {
  for await (const chunk of uiStream) {
    console.log("chunk:", JSON.stringify(chunk));
  }
  console.log(`\nTotal onError calls: ${calls}`);
}

main();
```

Run:
```
pnpm tsx repro.ts
```

Results:
```
  Observed output

  === onError call #1 ===
  Trace: stack
      at onError (repro.ts:…)
      at Object.transform (…/ai/src/generate-text/stream-text.ts:2402:28)

  === onError call #2 ===
  Trace: stack
      at onError (repro.ts:…)
      at <anonymous> (…/ai/src/ui/process-ui-message-stream.ts:710:15)
      at runUpdateMessageJob (…/ai/src/ui-message-stream/handle-ui-message-stream-finish.ts:97:11)
      at Object.transform (…/ai/src/ui/process-ui-message-stream.ts:104:15)

  Total onError calls: 2
```
Stack trace shows the handoff chain: `toUIMessageStream → handleUIMessageStreamFinish (runUpdateMessageJob) → processUIMessageStream.`

### Results

Two distinct call sites share the same onError reference:

1. Formatter stage in [generate-text/stream-text.ts](https://github.com/vercel/ai/blob/87d17235e9f673dcfe61cc28d25dab2b278dcea2/packages/ai/src/generate-text/stream-text.ts#L2502):
```ts
  case 'error': {
    controller.enqueue({
      type: 'error',
      errorText: onError(part.error),
    });
  }
```
Called synchronously with the original provider error; return value is written onto the outgoing chunk.
2. Notifier stage in [ui/process-ui-message-stream.ts](https://github.com/vercel/ai/blob/87d17235e9f673dcfe61cc28d25dab2b278dcea2/packages/ai/src/ui/process-ui-message-stream.ts#L835):
```ts
case 'error': {
onError?.(new Error(chunk.errorText));
}
```
2. Called with a freshly constructed Error wrapping the string Stage 1 just returned; return value is discarded.

The handoff is wired in `ui-message-stream/handle-ui-message-stream-finish.ts`, which forwards `onError` from `toUIMessageStream` into `processUIMessageStream`. This path
is only taken when `onFinish` or `onStepFinish` is passed to `toUIMessageStream`; otherwise Stage 2 is skipped.

### Proposal
Docs-only change. Add a note on the `onError` parameter of `toUIMessageStream`:

> May be invoked more than once per error: once by the formatter stage producing the SSE chunk's errorText, and again by the chunk walker as a notification (return value discarded). Side effects inside onError (logging, metrics, persistence) should be idempotent, or externally deduped — otherwise a single upstream error will produce duplicate records.


