### Description

`@ai-sdk/anthropic` auto-injects `anthropic-beta: effort-2025-11-24` into every request whenever `providerOptions.anthropic.effort` is set. The `effort` parameter [went GA on 2025-11-24 with no beta header required](https://platform.claude.com/docs/en/build-with-claude/effort) — only the `output_config.effort` body field is needed. The legacy header is now stale and is rejected by Vertex AI's strict-replica validator with HTTP 400:

```
{"type":"error","error":{"type":"invalid_request_error","message":"Unexpected value(s) `effort-2025-11-24` for the `anthropic-beta` header. Please consult our documentation at docs.anthropic.com or try again without the header."}}
```

This breaks every `effort`-using request through `createVertexAnthropic` once Vertex tightens validation (which is happening progressively across regions). Direct Anthropic still tolerates the stale value, so this surfaces only on Vertex.

### Root cause

In [`packages/anthropic/src/anthropic-language-model.ts`](https://github.com/vercel/ai/blob/main/packages/anthropic/src/anthropic-language-model.ts) (≈ line 707):

```ts
if (anthropicOptions?.effort) {
  betas.add('effort-2025-11-24');
}
```

The `output_config.effort` body field is what actually drives the feature server-side. The header is redundant and now rejected.

### Reproduction

**Credential-free** — confirms the SDK injects the stale header on a minimal request:

```ts
import { createAnthropic } from '@ai-sdk/anthropic';
import { generateText } from 'ai';

const provider = createAnthropic({
  apiKey: 'fake',
  fetch: async (url, init) => {
    console.log('anthropic-beta:', init?.headers['anthropic-beta']);
    return new Response('{}', { status: 200 });
  },
});

await generateText({
  model: provider('claude-opus-4-5'),
  prompt: 'hi',
  providerOptions: { anthropic: { effort: 'medium' } },
}).catch(() => {});

// Output:
// anthropic-beta: effort-2025-11-24
```

**End-to-end on Vertex** — same `providerOptions` path against `createVertexAnthropic` returns the 400 quoted above:

```ts
import { createVertexAnthropic } from '@ai-sdk/google-vertex/anthropic';
import { generateText } from 'ai';

const provider = createVertexAnthropic({ project: '...', location: '...' });

await generateText({
  model: provider('claude-opus-4-5@20251101'),
  prompt: 'hi',
  providerOptions: { anthropic: { effort: 'medium' } },
});
// → AI_APICallError: Unexpected value(s) `effort-2025-11-24` for the `anthropic-beta` header.
```

The server still receives `output_config: { effort: 'medium' }` in the body and would happily honor it. Only the header is the problem.

### Suggested fix

Stop auto-injecting `effort-2025-11-24`, mirroring the precedent set by [#14542](https://github.com/vercel/ai/pull/14542) which removed the analogous stale `fine-grained-tool-streaming-2025-05-14` header when *that* feature went GA. The body-field path (`output_config.effort`) is already wired and continues to work end-to-end on direct Anthropic, Bedrock, and Vertex.

The same reasoning likely applies to `task-budgets-2026-03-13`, `fast-mode-2026-02-01`, and `structured-outputs-2025-11-13` once each GA's, but `effort-2025-11-24` is the one currently breaking Vertex traffic.

