## Summary

`@ai-sdk/xai`'s Responses provider throws `UnsupportedFunctionalityError` for any file part whose `mediaType` does not start with `image/`, even when the caller provides a public HTTPS URL — but xAI's Responses API itself fully supports non-image documents (PDF, plain text, CSV, etc.) via `{ type: 'input_file', file_url }`.

This makes it impossible to use `xai.responses(...)` with PDFs through the AI SDK today, which is the headline use case demonstrated in xAI's own docs.

## Reproduction

```ts
import { createXai } from '@ai-sdk/xai';
import { generateText } from 'ai';

const xai = createXai({ apiKey: process.env.XAI_API_KEY! });

const result = await generateText({
  model: xai.responses('grok-4-fast'),
  messages: [
    {
      role: 'user',
      content: [
        { type: 'text', text: 'Summarize this document.' },
        {
          type: 'file',
          mediaType: 'application/pdf',
          data: new URL('https://docs.x.ai/assets/api-examples/documents/sales-report.txt'),
        },
      ],
    },
  ],
});
```

Throws:

```
AI_UnsupportedFunctionalityError: 'file part media type application/pdf' functionality not supported.
```

## Expected behavior

xAI's [Chat with Files](https://docs.x.ai/docs/guides/chat-with-files) docs show this exact shape working through `/v1/responses`:

```json
{
  "type": "input_file",
  "file_url": "https://docs.x.ai/assets/api-examples/documents/sales-report.txt"
}
```

The provider should serialize a non-image file part with URL data as `{ type: 'input_file', file_url: '<url>' }` instead of throwing.

## Root cause

[`convert-to-xai-responses-input.ts`](https://github.com/vercel/ai/blob/main/packages/xai/src/responses/convert-to-xai-responses-input.ts):

```ts
case 'file': {
  if (block.mediaType.startsWith('image/')) {
    // ...emits input_image
  } else {
    throw new UnsupportedFunctionalityError({
      functionality: `file part media type ${block.mediaType}`,
    });
  }
}
```

There is no branch for non-image files, even though the underlying `XaiResponsesUserMessageContentPart` type would just need a small extension to accept `file_url`. Additionally, `xai-responses-language-model.ts`'s `supportedUrls` only whitelists `image/*`, so PDF URLs get downloaded to bytes by the SDK before ever reaching the converter — which means even if the converter knew how to handle URLs, it would never see one.

## Proposed fix

PR submitted: #14805

- Extend `XaiResponsesUserMessageContentPart` to include `{ type: 'input_file'; file_url: string }`.
- In the converter, when a file part has `data: URL` and a non-image media type, emit `{ type: 'input_file', file_url }`.
- Add `application/pdf` and `text/*` to `supportedUrls` so URLs are passed through.
- Inline-byte (base64) inputs for non-image media types continue to throw (xAI Responses requires URL or Files API `file_id` for non-image documents); error message updated to point callers in the right direction.

## Workaround until merged

Either:

1. Route PDFs to a different provider (Gemini/OpenAI both work fine with `{ type: 'file', mediaType: 'application/pdf', data: URL }` through their AI SDK providers).
2. Skip the AI SDK and call `https://api.x.ai/v1/responses` directly with the documented `input_file` shape.

## Environment

- `@ai-sdk/xai`: 3.0.83 (latest at time of report)
- `ai`: 6.0.168
- Node 22

### Description

**Background**

The OpenAI Responses API supports stateful context via `previousResponseId`, removing the need to send full message history on each turn. However, when building a manual agentic loop with `stopWhen: stepCountIs(1)`, there is no way to submit a tool result for the next step while staying on the `previousResponseId` chain.

**Current behaviour**

To submit a tool result after manual execution, the only option is to fall back to `messages` (a `ToolModelMessage`) alongside `result.response.messages`. This forces the caller to reconstruct partial message history and drops the `previousResponseId` chain for that step — defeating the purpose of server-side state management.

**Desired behaviour**

Allow tool results to be passed via `providerOptions.openai` so the provider can translate them into `function_call_output` items in the Responses API `input`, combined with `previous_response_id`:

```ts
await generateText({
  model: openai.responses("gpt-4o"),
  prompt: "",
  tools: { myTool },
  stopWhen: stepCountIs(1),
  providerOptions: {
    openai: {
      previousResponseId: responseIdFromPriorStep,
      toolResults: [
        { callId: "call_abc123", output: JSON.stringify(myResult) }
      ]
    }
  }
});
```

The provider would translate this to:

```json
{
  "model": "gpt-4o",
  "previous_response_id": "resp_xxx",
  "input": [
    {
      "type": "function_call_output",
      "call_id": "call_abc123",
      "output": "..."
    }
  ]
}
```

**Use case**

Manual agentic loops where the caller orchestrates tool execution externally (e.g. async jobs, human review, external APIs) and wants to use `previousResponseId` throughout to avoid managing message history.

