### Description

## Summary

The Amazon Bedrock provider auto-downloads URL-sourced images and converts them to base64 when they appear as `image` parts in user-message content (since Bedrock requires base64), but throws `AI_UnsupportedFunctionalityError: 'unsupported tool content part type: image-url'` when the same kind of URL appears inside `tool-result` content. The two code paths are asymmetric without an obvious reason — the SDK already has all the machinery to make them consistent.

## Reproduction

```ts
import { generateText, tool } from "ai"
import { createAmazonBedrock } from "@ai-sdk/amazon-bedrock"
import { z } from "zod"

const bedrock = createAmazonBedrock({ region: "us-east-2" })

const PreviewImagesTool = tool({
  description: "Render preview images of a document",
  inputSchema: z.object({ documentId: z.string() }),
})

// User-message URL: works (SDK auto-downloads + base64s)
await generateText({
  model: bedrock("us.anthropic.claude-sonnet-4-6"),
  messages: [
    {
      role: "user",
      content: [
        { type: "image", image: new URL("https://example.com/img.png"), mediaType: "image/png" },
        { type: "text", text: "describe the image" },
      ],
    },
  ],
})
// ✓ succeeds

// Tool-result URL: throws
await generateText({
  model: bedrock("us.anthropic.claude-sonnet-4-6"),
  tools: { preview_images: PreviewImagesTool },
  messages: [
    { role: "user", content: [{ type: "text", text: "preview the doc" }] },
    {
      role: "assistant",
      content: [
        {
          type: "tool-call",
          toolCallId: "tc_1",
          toolName: "preview_images",
          input: { documentId: "abc" },
        },
      ],
    },
    {
      role: "tool",
      content: [
        {
          type: "tool-result",
          toolCallId: "tc_1",
          toolName: "preview_images",
          output: {
            type: "content",
            value: [
              { type: "text", text: "Here is the preview:" },
              { type: "image-url", url: "https://example.com/img.png" },
            ],
          },
        },
      ],
    },
    { role: "user", content: [{ type: "text", text: "describe it" }] },
  ],
})
// ✗ AI_UnsupportedFunctionalityError: 'unsupported tool content part type: image-url' functionality not supported.
```

## Expected behavior

The SDK should handle `image-url` (and ideally `file-url`) inside `tool-result` content the same way it handles URL-sourced `image` parts in user-message content: download via `downloadAssets` / the model's `supportedUrls` contract, then emit as a Bedrock `image` block with base64 bytes. Anything Bedrock can't accept natively (like URL sources, which it doesn't accept at all) should be downloaded and re-emitted by the SDK — exactly as it already does in the user-message path.

## Actual behavior

In `convertToBedrockChatMessages`, the tool-result branch is a hardcoded switch that only knows about `text` and `image-data`. Everything else throws:

```ts
// node_modules/@ai-sdk/amazon-bedrock/dist/index.mjs, lines 485–518
case "tool": {
  for (const part of content) {
    // ...
    switch (output.type) {
      case "content": {
        toolResultContent = output.value.map((contentPart) => {
          switch (contentPart.type) {
            case "text":      return { text: contentPart.text };
            case "image-data": return { image: { ..., source: { bytes: contentPart.data } } };
            default: {
              throw new UnsupportedFunctionalityError2({
                functionality: `unsupported tool content part type: ${contentPart.type}`
              });
            }
          }
        });
        // ...
```

Compare with the parallel user-message branch around line 445 that already handles URL data (because `downloadAssets` ran upstream and converted URLs to bytes). The Anthropic-flavored Bedrock entry point (`@ai-sdk/amazon-bedrock/anthropic`) hits the same dead-end, because `downloadAssets` only filters to `role === "user"` messages and never gets a chance to bridge URLs in tool-result content.

For contrast, `@ai-sdk/anthropic`'s `AnthropicMessagesLanguageModel` does handle this consistently — it has an explicit `case "image-url"` branch in its tool-result handler (`@ai-sdk/anthropic/dist/internal/index.js` around line 2205) that emits an Anthropic URL source, and `supportedUrls` covers `image/*` and `application/pdf`.


