### Description

## Feature request: behavioral trust scoring for tool calls + x402 payment gating

### Problem

The AI SDK's tool calling and MCP integration lets agents call external servers. Currently there's no runtime mechanism to evaluate whether a tool server is behaving normally *right now*. A server that was reliable yesterday could be timing out, returning anomalous data, or exhibiting latency spikes today. Static allow-lists can't catch behavioral drift.

This is especially relevant for the AI SDK because of the **x402 payment protocol integration** — when agents make paid tool calls, behavioral trust scoring becomes the gate between "should I pay for this call" and "this server looks degraded, hold settlement."

### Proposal

Integrate optional **runtime behavioral trust scoring** via the [Dominion Observatory](https://dominion-observatory.sgdata.workers.dev) (14,800+ MCP servers tracked, anonymized telemetry). Two integration surfaces:

**1. Tool call trust gate (before/after hook)**

```typescript
import { generateText } from 'ai';
import { query } from '@dominion/trust-provider';

const result = await generateText({
  model: openai('gpt-4'),
  tools: { webSearch, codeExec },
  toolCallMiddleware: async (toolCall, next) => {
    const trust = await query(toolCall.serverUrl);
    if (trust.decision === 'FAIL') {
      throw new Error('Tool blocked: trust score too low');
    }
    return next(toolCall);
  },
});
```

**2. x402 beforeSettle hook (payment gating)**

```typescript
import { createObservatoryProvider, beforeSettle } from '@dominion/trust-provider';

const config = {
  providers: [createObservatoryProvider()],
  policy: { kind: 'strict' },
  failureMode: 'fail-closed',
};

const result = await beforeSettle(trustQuery, config);
if (result.decision === 'PASS') {
  // proceed with x402 payment settlement
}
```

### Why this matters for the AI SDK

- **x402 payment flows**: The AI SDK is positioned for paid tool calls. Behavioral trust scoring is the missing gate — you don't want to settle payment to a server exhibiting anomalous behavior. The beforeSettle hook in @dominion/trust-provider was designed for exactly this.
- **MCP server ecosystem**: As more MCP servers come online, the quality variance grows. Runtime trust scoring separates the reliable servers from the degraded ones.
- **TypeScript-native**: The @dominion/trust-provider npm package is TypeScript-first with full type exports, designed for the AI SDK's ecosystem.

### Existing infrastructure

- **Observatory**: live at dominion-observatory.sgdata.workers.dev, 14,800+ servers, 87,000+ interactions
- **npm package**: @dominion/trust-provider — TypeScript SDK with query(), beforeSettle(), advisoryHeaders()
- **x402 integration**: [PR #2300](https://github.com/x402-foundation/x402/pull/2300) adds trust-provider extension to x402 protocol
- **DID-based identity**: payer.agent_id as did:web: URI for cryptographic agent identity binding
- **Privacy**: only anonymized telemetry. No prompts, tool arguments, outputs, or user data.

### References

- [Dominion Observatory](https://dominion-observatory.sgdata.workers.dev)
- [@dominion/trust-provider source](https://github.com/vdineshk/daee-engine/tree/main/packages/trust-provider)
- [x402 Trust-Provider Interface spec](https://github.com/vdineshk/daee-engine/blob/main/specs/x402-trust-provider-interface/v0.1/SPEC.md)
