### Description

Vertex MaaS Llama 4 responses can complete with no text when no `max_tokens` or `max_completion_tokens` value is sent by the provider.

Adding a `fetch` shim that injects `max_tokens: 4096` into the outgoing OpenAI-compatible request body makes the same prompt return content.

### Reproduction

```ts
import { createVertexMaas } from '@ai-sdk/google-vertex/maas';
import { generateText, streamText } from 'ai';

const project = process.env.GOOGLE_VERTEX_PROJECT!;

const provider = createVertexMaas({
  project,
  location: 'us-east5',
  baseURL:
    `https://us-east5-aiplatform.googleapis.com/v1/projects/${project}/locations/us-east5/endpoints/openapi`,
});

const result = await generateText({
  model: provider('meta/llama-4-scout-17b-16e-instruct-maas'),
  prompt: 'Reply with exactly ok',
});

console.log({
  text: result.text,
  finishReason: result.finishReason,
});
```

Observed result without a max token value:

```json
{
  "text": "",
  "finishReason": "stop"
}
```

Control workaround:

```ts
const provider = createVertexMaas({
  project,
  location: 'us-east5',
  baseURL:
    `https://us-east5-aiplatform.googleapis.com/v1/projects/${project}/locations/us-east5/endpoints/openapi`,
  fetch: async (url, init) => {
    if (init?.body && typeof init.body === 'string') {
      const body = JSON.parse(init.body);
      if (body.max_tokens === undefined && body.max_completion_tokens === undefined) {
        return fetch(url, {
          ...init,
          body: JSON.stringify({ ...body, max_tokens: 4096 }),
        });
      }
    }

    return fetch(url, init);
  },
});
```

With that workaround in place, the same model/prompt returns content.

### Expected behavior

The provider should either set a reasonable default max token value for Vertex MaaS Llama requests, map AI SDK defaults into `max_tokens`, or document that `maxOutputTokens` / `max_tokens` is required for this provider/model family.

### Actual behavior

The request can return `finishReason: "stop"` with empty text and no error.

