## Description

`@ai-sdk/mcp` (tested with 1.0.46/1.0.47) only processes SSE events whose parsed `event` type is strictly the string `"message"`:

```js
// dist/index.js (HTTP transport, POST response handling and inbound SSE)
const { event, data } = value;
if (event === "message") { ... }
```

`eventsource-parser` leaves the `event` field `undefined` when the SSE frame has no explicit `event:` line. Per the [SSE specification](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/server-sent-events.html#dispatchMessage), an event without an `event:` field must be dispatched as a `message` event:

> If the data buffer is not the empty string ... Initialize event's type attribute to "message" ... If the event type buffer has a value other than the empty string, change the type of the newly created event to equal the value of the event type buffer.

Several MCP server implementations/proxies (e.g. [agentgateway](https://github.com/agentgateway/agentgateway)) reply to streamable-HTTP POSTs with `Content-Type: text/event-stream` bodies containing bare `data:` frames:

```
data: {"jsonrpc":"2.0","id":1,"result":{...}}
```

The client silently drops these events, so the `request()` promise for `initialize` / `tools/list` never settles — `experimental_createMCPClient(...)` and `client.tools()` hang forever with no error. This is particularly nasty in server-side use (the calling HTTP request hangs indefinitely).

## Reproduction

Minimal server that mimics this framing:

```js
import http from 'http';
import { experimental_createMCPClient as createMCPClient } from '@ai-sdk/mcp';

const server = http.createServer((req, res) => {
  let body = '';
  req.on('data', c => (body += c));
  req.on('end', () => {
    const msg = JSON.parse(body);
    if (!('id' in msg)) return res.writeHead(202).end();
    res.writeHead(200, { 'Content-Type': 'text/event-stream' });
    res.end(`data: ${JSON.stringify({
      jsonrpc: '2.0',
      id: msg.id,
      result: {
        protocolVersion: msg.params?.protocolVersion ?? '2025-06-18',
        capabilities: {},
        serverInfo: { name: 'fake', version: '0.0.1' },
      },
    })}\n\n`);
  });
});
server.listen(3999);

// Hangs forever:
await createMCPClient({ name: 'test', transport: { type: 'http', url: 'http://localhost:3999/mcp' } });
```

## Expected behavior

Events without an explicit `event:` field are treated as `message` events:

```js
if (event === undefined || event === "message") { ... }
```

(applies to the three SSE read loops: legacy SSE transport, HTTP transport POST response streams, and the inbound standalone SSE stream)

For comparison, the official `@modelcontextprotocol/sdk` and the Go (`mark3labs/mcp-go`) clients handle bare-`data:` frames fine.

## Workaround

We currently ship a `yarn patch` applying the change above.

